<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="1a7d0ff">&lt;p&gt;
    Start by defining an overall approach to handling change on the project based on the required level of formality and
    level of collaboration with key stakeholders and the project team.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Identify the different types of changes likely to be encountered and set any thresholds for each type along with their
    associated workflow and allowable states.&amp;nbsp; Include any limitations on types&amp;nbsp;or number of changes along with
    identifying who can submit changes requests.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="6bfd34ce"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="a2383840"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="fc3cef40"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="1c25399f">The purpose of this task is to make sure that proper level of change management procedures are utilized by the project in
order to prevent unauthorized changes without over burdening the project team.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="7f9f91a"></attribute>
</Element>
